  books that influence the series in The  Last of Us Part One Ellie carries a book  with her in the Lakeside Resort section  of the game the book is titled to get to  the other side written by Catherine  McCormick McCormick is a reference to  Cormac McCarthy the author of The  Pulitzer winning book the road the road  is the story of a father and son that  travel across a post-apocalyptic United  States two references to another book  round out the two major literary  influences Behind The Last of Us in The  Last of Us Part One a newspaper clipping  artifact that Joel and Ellie find in the  University section of the game lists the  journalist as Lev benioff this is a  reference to the 2008 book city of  Thieves written by David benioff  showrunner and writer of Game of Thrones  and features a protagonist named Lev the  connection to City of Thieves is  strengthened further during Abby's  portion of The Last of Us Part 2. during  Abby's section of Seattle day one she  wakes up after having fallen asleep  while reading city of Thieves and as  stated before Lev is the main character  of the novel novel which mirrors the  name of the young seraphite kid Lev who  becomes a major player in Abby's  character Arc  number 7 The Naughty Dog verse naughty  dog has placed references to its other  franchises inside The Last of Us games  here are a few standouts right after  meeting Henry and Sam you can find plush  toys based off of Nathan Drake Jack and  Daxter these are located in the child's  room in the serenity Apartments Jack and  Daxter up on the dresser and Nathan  Drake is on the bed similar to the plush  toys in the choo choo toy store a few  Uncharted and Jack and Daxter board  games are nestled into the far corner on  a shelf in Pittsburgh you can find a pub  named o'sullivans this is a referencing  Victor Sullivan of the Uncharted games  and B if you go inside it looks almost  identical to the pub at the beginning of  Uncharted 3 Drake's Deception right  outside O'Sullivan's as well as outside  the arcade and left behind sits Java  Jack a coffee cart referencing Jack from  Jack and Daxter in the Halloween store  and left behind Ellie finds both  Uncharted and Jack and Daxter themed  costumes the arcade in Left Behind is  called raja's arcade this is in  reference to Eddie and Rika Raja from  the Uncharted series games the Jack X  combat racing arcade game that is out of  order in raja's arcade is a reference to  the PS2 game of the same name in The  Last of Us Part 2 both Ellie and Eugene  have PS3s which also appear all over the  series in the mess hall Abby's friend  Jordan is playing the fire Canyon  section of Jack and Daxter the precursor  Legacy on Evita in the Westlake Bank in  downtown Seattle inside a security  deposit box is a ring with the  inscription sick parwas Magna this is  the seminal ring that belongs to Nathan  Drake in the Uncharted series  number six Don't Stop Me Now in The Last  of Us Part One On The Wall next to the  toy store there's a poster that says I  want to ride my bicycle with an image of  a top hat and a bike this is a reference  to the 1978 song Bicycle Race by Queen  number five not today capitalism in The  Last of Us Part One there are some  corporate mascots that represent much  Bleaker versions of their real-life  counterparts one very notable example is  the game of strife on the second floor  of the ranch house there is a board game  box labeled the game of strife this is a  much more somber version of the real  life board game the game of life  Number Four The Legend of ish throughout  the Last of Us Part One you can find a  selection of notes and artifacts hinting  at the lives of previous residents of  the areas you Traverse none leads you  down as intense a rabbit hole as the  resident of the sewers known as ish ish  did not start in the sewers in  Pittsburgh the first note you find from  him details that he was living on a  trawling boat and was away at Sea when  the outbreak occurred after running out  of supplies ish ran his motor ground  near the sewers and created a safe house  in them again running low in supplies he  scavenged the nearby suburbs where he  encountered Susan Kyle and their kids  ish offered them safety in the sewers  and they joined him to create a larger  Community branching off of his existing  Safe House the community thrived for a  while and grew to include Dany ish and  Danny served as the Protectors of The  Refuge salvaging weapons and armor off  of dead soldiers in the area during this  time we get the only depiction of ish as  drawn by one of the children in the camp  the piece would not last however the  door to the community was left open by  an unknown someone allowing a horde of  infected to clean out most of the camp  ish Susan and some of the children from  the community were able to escape into  the suburbs their whereabouts as of the  time of The Last of Us Part One are  unknown although this story is pieced  together through found artifacts and  notes the story of ish is not an  entirely original one ish is thought to  be a reference to isherwood ish Williams  the main character in the novel Earth  abides from 1949. in the novel Williams  creates a community of pandemic  survivors and is also a sailor with his  name being another reference to Ishmael  the main protagonist from Moby Dick  three movie Magic throughout the Last of  Us Parts one and two Visual and spoken  references to real life movies pop up  again and again in The Last of Us Part  One as Ellie and Joel explore the  serenity Apartments they can shiv open a  locked room that contains fictional  representations of real-life films these  include hair trigger referencing the  transporter the season of Vengeance  referencing the film The Last Samurai  and the lost kingdom which is in  reference to the Indiana Jones franchise  along with these posters the film dawn  of the wolf appears in many different  places throughout the Last of Us Part  One from its first appearance in Sarah's  bedroom to Billboards and movie posters  this fictional horror romance is a  direct reference to the Twilight series  in The Last of Us Part 2 in the Westlake  Bank Dina and Ellie discuss a movie with  Surfer bank robbers a reference to the  film Point Break starring the  illustrious Keanu Reeves in Abby's  section very early on Manny mentions  that he wants to watch a movie until he  passes out when Mel questions him about  which movie he's going to pick he States  he's going to watch a film where a girl  rides on a wolf due to his previous  admission of being an anime fan it's  highly probable that Manny is going to  watch one of my favorite movies of all  time Princess Mononoke  number 2 the 0451 code during Ellie's  first day in Seattle the gate code for  gate West 2 is 0451 this code pops up in  games such as System Shock System Shock  2 Bioshock Dishonored and thief the Dark  Project the code itself is an in  reference to the code used to get into  the offices of Looking Glass Studios  developers of system shocks 1 2 and  Thief it's important to know that  Naughty Dog are not the only Studio to  use this reference Looking Glass Studios  is so beloved by developers that this  code has appeared in at least 20 games  some that use the key code and some that  don't even have keypad technology in  them  number one The Last of Us Vice in the  same section that Ellie hunts down Nora  in the hospital on her day two in  Seattle the first combat encounter you  have upon entering the hospital is with  a young guard playing their Vita what  game are they so lost in Hotline Miami  another story of Revenge and Desperation  the hidden secrets in Easter eggs inside  The Last of Us series are as richly  cultivated and layered as the  performances and environments that  naughty dog has created I love that they  can make references to their own IPS as  well as other references in pop culture  while maintaining the tone and  atmosphere of The Last of Us we'll have  to see if the Last of Us Part One remake  hides any more treats for everything  else video games keep it here at  GameSpot

